ven-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Thollesson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Andersson</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional divergence and horizontal transfer of type IV secretion systems</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><year>2005</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>1325</fpage><lpage>1336</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15746011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heller</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Riegel</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hansmann</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Delacour</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bermond</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Dehio</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title><italic>Bartonella tribocorum</italic> sp. nov., a new <italic>Bartonella</italic> species isolated from the blood of wild rats</article-title><source>Int J Syst Bacteriol</source><year>1998</year><volume>48</volume><issue>Part 4</issue><fpage>1333</fpage><lpage>1339</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9828434</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kempf</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Volkmann</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Schaller</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sander</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Alitalo</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Riess</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Autenrieth</surname><given-names>IB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence of a leading role for VEGF in <italic>Bartonella henselae</italic>-induced endoth